WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.625
So what we often say is that, look,

2
00:00:01.625 --> 00:00:04.314
there are three ways to align
these competencies, if you will.

3
00:00:04.314 --> 00:00:06.275
One is, develop them.

4
00:00:06.275 --> 00:00:10.336
Give them the opportunity to accelerate
their development so that they can

5
00:00:10.336 --> 00:00:12.906
outperform in the seat that
they're being asked to fill.

6
00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:15.784
The second is you layer them.

7
00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:18.561
You bring on talent that can
actually upgrade, if you will,

8
00:00:18.561 --> 00:00:22.987
the skills needed in the organization,
slightly more expensive than development,

9
00:00:22.987 --> 00:00:26.978
but still valuable because that
person becomes potentially a catalyst,

10
00:00:26.978 --> 00:00:30.659
if you will. And then the last one,
which is obviously the most expensive,

11
00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:31.842
and that's hire and fire.

12
00:00:32.468 --> 00:00:35.911
Right? But if you don't
make those decisions,

13
00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:40.379
the rest of the organization doesn't
believe you in terms of your,

14
00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:42.913
if you will, commitment to that strategy,

15
00:00:42.913 --> 00:00:46.914
because they're dealing with people who
are potentially not competent for the

16
00:00:46.914 --> 00:00:48.484
priorities you've assigned to them.

